  "fixed_acceptance_rules": {
    "R1_pp_higher_better": "candidate - baseline >= -0.2 pp (gate02 TOL_PP; judge(): d=(a-b)*sign; d < -0.2 -> REGRESSION). Applies to every metric expressed in % / P / R / F1 with sign +1.",
    "R2_pp_lower_better": "candidate - baseline <= +0.2 pp (sign -1: old-site ghost %, TUM contamination %, synthetic rows whose name contains MAD/residual/latency/lost/FP/ID switches/RMSE and are in %).",
    "R3_count_strings": "Object/Change/D2/D3 TP/FP/FN strings: identical -> pass. Different -> queue.sh gate STOPs; ACCEPTANCE docs accept only strictly-better counts (TP not lower, FP and FN not higher, at least one improved: e.g. 3RScan scene3 FP 1->0). Any worse or mixed change -> fail.",
    "R4_other_numeric": "non-pp numbers (MAD cm, latency s, cell counts, residual cm): gate02 lists them as CHECK for a human decision and queue.sh does not stop on them -> recorded, not pass/fail.",
    "R5_bonn": "the 4 wanted verdicts (moving: start cleared / end present; placing: end present; removing: start cleared) must equal the baseline verdicts or improve NO->YES; fractions are recorded only (ACCEPTANCE_final_23e3a3c.md section 4).",
    "R6_3rscan": "D3 TP/FP/FN by R3; geometry P/R/F1 @5/10/20 by R1 (the acceptance docs compare them; type rule).",
    "R7_tum": "person contamination % by R2 (23e3a3c passed with +0.09 pp \"within 0.2\").",
    "R8_no_compensation": "a better cell never offsets a failing cell (user code-review rule A3: a higher total geometric F1 does not offset degradation of state/history/ghost).",
    "R9_gate_cells": "real A/B/C cells are exactly compare_cand.real_cells(): Object P/R/F1 (duration-weighted NR), Object raw native F1, Change D2 F1 + TP/FP/FN, Change D3 F1 + TP/FP/FN (b,c), Old-site ghost % (b,c), G1 F1@5, P@5, R@5, F1@10, F1@20, G2 F1@5. synthetic = all rows of FULL_RESULTS_ours.csv (97)."
  },
